WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.869
-I'm so happy.
-I am so happy.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.238
-I am a giant --
I'm a big fan and I love you,

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.239
so I'm so happy
you're here in person.

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:08.507
Oh, my gosh.
Thank you for being --

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:10.109
-I'm so happy, Jimmy,
to be here.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.712
-Thank you so much.
"No Time to Die" is finally out.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.113
-Yes.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.916
-I think Daniel Craig was on
our show twice promoting it,

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.551
and it kept getting...
-I'm a bit jealous.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.052
-...pushed.
No, oh, my gosh.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:21.921
Please come back.
But I mean --

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:24.224
Now it's finally out,
and I got to see it,

00:00:24.224 --> 00:00:26.025
and you are fantastic
in this film.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.059
-Well, thank you.

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.294
-It is a -- it's a beautiful --

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.729
I mean, obviously,
it's a James Bond film,

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:30.864
so there's action.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.665
It's a thriller.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.333
It's spy.
You don't know anything.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.402
It's just gorgeously shot.

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.771
And then it's just --
it's just everything.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.039
It's the whole package.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.442
I don't think they make movies
like this anymore.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.676
I mean, there's --

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.912
nothing against movies with CGI
and all that,

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:49.449
but you could tell
these are real stunts

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.551
and real people
doing these stunts,

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.920
and it's like, if you do two
takes of this, like,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.388
"Oh, this is gonna cost us."

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.622
[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.125
It's like, "Let's just please do
one take of this."

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.827
Do you get nervous if you have
a big explosion or something,

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:03.762
like if you mess up a line
or something?

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:05.498
-Oh, yeah.
I'm very nervous.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.799
-You are?
-Yeah, always.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.334
-Really?
-Yeah. You can tell, no?

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.401
Look, I'm so red.

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:11.170
-No!
You don't -- I hear you.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.539
You're gorgeous.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.640
-Thank you.
-Here's you on the red carpet.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.443
This is at the London premiere
of "No Time to Die."

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.712
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah, that's hype.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.714
Come on.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:25.418
Now at the premiere,
the Royal Family were there.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.821
-Yeah, yeah.
We were in the box with them.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.221
-And what did it feel like?

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:30.356
-It was really nice,

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:32.492
because, you know, finally
the film came out

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:35.728
and we had to postpone
several times.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:41.033
So, to feel the excitement
in the theater was great.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.535
-I -- Yeah.
-It was just -- Yeah.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.304
-And had you seen any cuts of
the film and stuff like --

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.473
or the final film before
that or...?

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:51.043
-So, I saw bits of it,
but it was the first time

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:53.513
that I really saw the film,
you know?

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:55.648
-In the theater.

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.483
-Yeah, yeah, it was great.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.552
-Just even at the beginning
when the --

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.654
[ Sings "James Bond Theme" ]

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:03.522
I'm like -- I almost
started crying right there.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:06.326
I was like, "Oh!"
I was so excited.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:09.929
-You've seen the film, but you
can't talk about it, right?

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.364
-I actually can't say anything.
-Yeah.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:12.765
And I would never do that.
I would never --

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.234
-Yeah. That's good.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.535
-[ French accent ] No spoiler.

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.437
-Yeah, no spoiler, please.
Don't say anything.

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:19.772
-[ Normal ] Yeah,
don't say anything.

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.540
But, I mean, can you maybe
tell us a little something

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.542
about the...?

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.977
-I mean, you've seen
the film, right?

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.178
-Yeah.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:28.180
-So, yeah, I can tell you
a few things,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.383
like, for example,
you know when --

00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:39.392
[ Speaking French ]

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.560
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:49.435
[ Speaking French ]

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:50.669
[ Smooches ]

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:53.205
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:54.741
I do remember that, yeah.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.543
Yeah, well, yeah, of course.
I do remember that part, yeah.

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.412
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
that was beautiful.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.813
Yeah, you didn't give
too much away.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.015
-A lot of action.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:04.984
-That's exactly how
you sum it up right there.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.318
You're phenomenal.

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:09.221
And I just thought
it was so interesting, too,

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:12.558
to be James Bond -- obviously
all of these movies,

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:15.995
but to be his love interest
in two movies.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.797
-Yeah.
-It's rare. You don't see that.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:18.831
-Yeah.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:22.034
-What did it feel like
coming back?

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.402
-I mean, she's --

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:28.174
This time, she's a more complex
woman, you know?

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.776
But she's a real woman.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:32.478
Like a simple woman.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:37.550
She has -- She had
a difficult upbringing.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:41.387
Her mother is an alcoholic.

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:44.657
Her father is an assassin.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.626
She falls in love with a killer.

00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:50.596
But she's a normal woman,
you know?

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:53.399
-[ Laughs ]
Everyone can relate, yeah.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.334
A lot of people can relate.
-You can relate to her easily.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:57.136
-But it is tricky, your role.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.639
And it's -- And when you see
this, you go like --

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.006
'cause I thought "Spectre," too.

00:04:01.006 --> 00:04:03.075
I go, "Ooh, that was good,
and it was tricky."

00:04:03.075 --> 00:04:04.343
But this one --
-Yeah, but "Spectre,"

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:05.411
we didn't really know her.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.613
She was more mysterious.
-Yeah.

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:09.882
-This time, we really
get to know her.

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.651
-You dive in and -- Oh, my gosh,
you're just phenomenal.

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:14.920
I'm so happy that you're here.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.523
Here's Léa Seydoux
and Daniel Craig

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.524
in "No Time to Die."

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.525
Take a look at this.

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:28.066 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:28.066 --> 00:04:29.402
-Open the door.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.638
Open the door!

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.207
Don't.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:36.008
-What is it?

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:38.277
-James, you...

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:42.181
you don't know what this is...
to bring me to this.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.516
Please.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:45.151
-All right, open the doors.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.485
Open the door.
-Open it.

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:47.820
[ Door beeps, unlocks ]

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:52.625
-Where are you going?

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:55.061
-Home.

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.466
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ooh!

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.368
Léa Seydoux, everybody!

